ersion":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":85520,"output_tokens":2141,"requests":4}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["3 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","AC item '[non-codebase] Every Tier-1/Tier-2 run appears in the committed ledger with actu' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox.","AC item '[non-codebase] `ledger.print_summary()` reports spent/remaining and the total ne' is [operator-attested] but its provenance declaration is incomplete (environment is missing (no provenance declaration found); principal is missing (no provenance declaration found); privilege_posture is missing (no provenance declaration found); instrument is missing (no provenance declaration found); justification is missing (no provenance declaration found)); add an indented continuation line 'provenance: environment=<v>; principal=<v>; privilege_posture=<production-equivalent|broader|narrower>; instrument=<live-call|simulation|static-analysis> — <justification>' under the checkbox."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that finalize()/reconcile() re-check cumulative ACTUAL spend after appending and raise or loudly warn when the just-finished run pushed committed spend past LEDGER_CAP_USD, so the cap guarantee survives an estimate underrun (not just the pre-flight estimate check).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6167,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reserve() gates on estimate: 'ledger.reserve(estimate) refuses ... when spent + estimate > cap_usd - reserve_usd'","finalize path is described only as 'the ledger row finalised with actual spend' / '(finalize()/reconcile() append committed rows)' — no actual-spend cap check","The plan itself frames reserve_usd as 'a safety margin against the gap between an estimate and a run's actual cost', acknowledging estimate<actual is possible, but nothing enforces that the overrun stays within the $30 reserve","PER_SAMPLE_ESTIMATE_USD is a FLAT historical estimate, so actual agentic spend can plausibly exceed it for a hot run"],"finding":"The cap is enforced only at pre-flight (reserve() checks the flat ESTIMATE against cap-reserve); finalize()/reconcile() append the run's ACTUAL priced spend with no cap re-check, so a run that costs more than its flat per-sample estimate can push cumulative committed spend past $200, absorbed only by the un-enforced $30 reserve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f05669620a1172370","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'reserve() refuses ... when spent + estimate > cap_usd - reserve_usd' and 'Metering — the ledger row finalised with actual spend'","norm_id":"n036b014bd3766fc6","priority":0.1833,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Tier-2 run estimated at 3.4*sample_n passes reserve() but its agentic loop runs long and actually costs materially more, and the committed ledger silently crosses $200 after finalize()","Several runs each modestly over their estimate accumulate past the cap with no signal at finalize time"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"After appending the finalized row, compute _spent_so_far() and, if it exceeds LEDGER_CAP_USD, raise a loud CapExceeded (or emit a prominent warning) — turning the reserve buffer into an enforced backstop rather than a passive margin. Add a unit test: a run whose actual priced spend crosses the cap surfaces loudly at finalize.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an ADR or design-doc/AGENTS.md note capturing the `ledger.jsonl` row schema and the $200 cap / $30 reserve invariant so downstream harness and `__main__` children have a durable contract reference.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e","T7"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"A committed ledger docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/ledger.jsonl: one row per eval run (run_id, tier, candidate, sample_n, ...)\"","\"cap_usd and reserve_usd are constants in the module (200 / 30), read from ONE place\"","Absence: no Scope entry adds/updates an ADR or design doc describing the ledger row schema or the cap invariant for downstream consumers."],"finding":"The plan introduces a new committed data contract (`ledger.jsonl` schema) and a new epic-wide $200 cap invariant, but names no ADR / AGENTS.md / design-doc update capturing this architectural decision — the mechanism is documented only inline in the ticket body, which future eval-harness children (`presolar-finable-binturong`, `peaceable-choppy-sapsucker`) and the Tier-0 `__main__` ticket will need to consume.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f10e3139c66ffaa18","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope (ledger.jsonl, LEDGER_CAP_USD/LEDGER_RESERVE_USD)","norm_id":"nad5d92326fa6973f","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later harness child needs the exact ledger row field set and cap-check contract but must reverse-engineer it from the ticket body or the module source."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a short design-doc/ADR entry under docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/ describing the ledger row fields, the finalize/reconcile lifecycle, and the LEDGER_CAP_USD/LEDGER_RESERVE_USD invariant; reference it from the Scope list.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how reconcile() detects an already-finalized run (e.g. keyed on run_id) so finalize()/reconcile() are idempotent, and add a unit test that running reconcile() twice (and reconcile() after a normal finalize()) does not append a duplicate ledger row or double-count spend.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a run that dies mid-way is finalised from whatever rows exist on the next ledger.reconcile() call.'","Plan documents the single-writer TOCTOU non-goal but does not address idempotency of finalize/reconcile themselves (a run finalized twice, or reconcile run twice).","Ledger spend feeds the cap check in reserve(); a duplicated finalized row would over-count spent and could spuriously refuse a valid run (or, if under-counted, defeat the cap)."],"finding":"reconcile() is specified to finalize 'a crashed run ... from whatever rows exist on the next ledger.reconcile() call,' but the plan never states how reconcile() distinguishes an already-finalized run from a genuinely-crashed one, nor whether re-running reconcile() (or reconcile() after a normal finalize()) is idempotent. If reconcile re-processes detail rows for a run that already has a committed ledger row, it could append a duplicate row and double-count spend against the cap.","group_criter